    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0359" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 195.2/1637a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-30T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7086. Russian steamers <hi rendition="#italic">Yaroslavl</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Novgorod</hi> are proceeding from White Sea and will
                    probably call at British port. They are among several ships of Russian Volunteer
                    Fleet now chartered to United States Shipping Board. Terms of agreement provide
                    they may be taken over either in British or American port. Please advise British
                    authorities at once. Shipping Board will give full instructions to London
                    representative.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
